Description: YouTube browser and player for the Trinity Desktop Environment
 TDE YouTube is a native Trinity (TDE) application to search, browse and
 watch YouTube videos without a web browser.
 .
 Search results are listed with thumbnails, duration, channel and view
 count. Videos play inside the window in an embedded mpv player, with
 play/pause, seeking, volume and full screen controls. Favourites and a
 watch history are kept locally, and the description of each video is
 shown next to the player.
 .
 yt-dlp is used to search YouTube and mpv to play the videos; no YouTube
 account or API key is needed. Because distribution packages of yt-dlp are
 usually too old for YouTube, TDE YouTube downloads the official portable
 yt-dlp and the QuickJS-ng JavaScript engine from their GitHub releases into
 the user's home folder, verifies them and keeps them up to date. This can
 be turned off in the settings, in which case the installed yt-dlp (and
 quickjs) are used. This program is not affiliated with YouTube or Google.
